#AREA The Cathedral of Waterdeep~

#AUTHORS Jaxom~

#RANGES 30 50 1 99

#HELPS
-1 CATHEDRAL_CHANGES~
01.02.05 - 72 Spelling Corrections. (Mag)
01.02.05 - Colored the area help files. (Mag)
01.02.05 - Reformatted quest text to consolidate speeches. (Mag)
01.02.05 - Added Sam, Joe, and digger to namelists of the grave digger mobs.
           This allows you to look at the mob by name instead of accidentally
           looking at the open grave. (Mag)
01.02.05 - Changed bride speech_prog i object to speech_prog p i object to prevent
           double spam. (Mag)
01.02.05 - Changed mpgoto 1, suicide in bride and gravediggers to mppurge $i. (Mag)
01.02.05 - Changed mppurge to mppurge gravediggermobtwo in gravediggermobone. (Mag)
01.02.05 - Fixed many room descriptions. (Mag)
01.02.05 - Changed door keywords behind altar to match room description. (Mag)
01.02.05 - Changed room 4375 to The Landing and removed noble. (Mag)
01.02.05 - Made 4375, 4303, 4302, 4374, and 4366, 4357 ROOM_NO_MOB. (Mag)
01.02.05 - Using quasimodo ethereal, the parishioners now pop at 7pm.  They self
           purge at 6am, spam and have a rand_prog to attack people in room. (Mag)
01.03.05 - Created rooms 4393, 4394, and 4395 as mob loading rooms. (Mag)
01.03.05 - Created mobs 4317, 4318, and 4319 and dispersed in respective areas. (Mag)
01.03.05 - Created item 4312 and placed one in each room of Noble's Balcony. (Mag)
~

-1 'THE CATHEDRAL OF WATERDEEP' CATHEDRAL~
{000}.{300}
{000} {300}{044}........................................................................{300}
{000} {300}{044}........................................................................{300}
{000} {300}{044}.......................{300}{074}The Cathedral of Waterdeep{300}{044}.......................{300}
{000} {300}{044}........................................................................{300}
{000} {300}{044}..{300}{074}The Cathedral of Waterdeep is one of the great wonders of the world.{300}{044}..{300}
{000} {300}{044}..{300}{074}Its architecture is a glorious mix of styles that people the realms{300}{044}...{300}
{000} {300}{044}..{300}{074}over admire and loathe.  Merchants and tradesmen congregate on the{300}{044}....{300}
{000} {300}{044}..{300}{074}steps of its main entrance off the Street of Silks.  It is rumored{300}{044}....{300}
{000} {300}{044}..{300}{074}the Archbishop seeks a young hero who would engage in a quest.{300}{044}........{300}
{000} {300}{044}........................................................................{300}
{000} {300}{044}..{300}{074}(a) Bishop Jaxom{300}{044}......................................................{300}
{000} {300}{044}..{300}{074}(b) Quests{300}{044}............................................................{300}
{000} {300}{044}........................................................................{300}
{000} {300}{044}........................................................................{300}
{000}.{300}

{a}JAXOM
{b}CATHEDRALQUESTS
~

-1 CATHEDRALQUESTS~
{000}.{300}
{000} {300}{044}......................................................................{300}
{000} {300}{044}......................................................................{300}
{000} {300}{044}.................{300}{074}Quests in the Cathedral of Waterdeep{300}{044}.................{300}
{000} {300}{044}......................................................................{300}
{000} {300}{044}..{300}{074}One quest in the Cathedral of Waterdeep is for level 50 equipment.{300}{044}..{300}
{000} {300}{044}..{300}{074}The path you choose during the quest determines if the equipment{300}{044}....{300}
{000} {300}{044}..{300}{074}you get is Anti-Good or Anti-Evil.  Another quest is for a pair of{300}{044}..{300}
{000} {300}{044}..{300}{074}level 20 rings.{300}{044}.....................................................{300}
{000} {300}{044}......................................................................{300}
{000} {300}{044}......................................................................{300}
{000}.{300}
~

0 $~

#MOBILES
#4300
worshipping commoner~
a worshipping commoner~
A commoner worships here.~
He wears simple linen clothes and looks like a normal Waterdhavian citizen.
~
ACT_RACE|ACT_BODY|ACT_SENTINEL|ACT_SMART AFF_TONGUES|AFF_UNDERSTAND 0 S
40 BODY_HAND|BODY_HEAD 0 1d1+631 1d1+26
10000 RACE_HUMAN
POS_STANDING POS_STANDING SEX_MALE

#4301
